  "description": "QISJOS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C8 H20 N1 O2 1+,C100 H200 Fe5 N8 O64 Pr8 1-,3(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr4B (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2B (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3B (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.448-4.341 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.46-117.27°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [FeIII5Pr8(μ3-OH)12(L)4(piv)12(NO3)4(OAc)4][H3L]·3CH2Cl2 (L = nBudea2−; piv = O2CCMe3); C111H226Cl6Fe5N9O66Pr8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Fe(III).",
